{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]A sabbath rest remains for [Eb]us
[Bb]Whoever enters stops their [Eb]works
[Gm7]Like God rested from [Eb]His own
Make every effort to go [Bb]on
So none fall by [F]disobedience
[Gm]Let us hold [Eb]fast to the promise
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]The word of God is liv[F]ing and active
[Gm7]Sharper than any two-[Eb]edged sword
It [Bb]pierces to the point where soul [F]and spirit divide
[Gm7]Judges the [F]thoughts and in[Eb]tentions of the [Bb]heart
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
No creature is hidden from Him
[Eb]Everything lies naked and [Gm7]exposed
Before the eyes of the [Eb]one
To whom we must give ac[Gm7]count
We have a great high [Eb]priest
Jesus the [Bb]Son of God [F]
[Gm]Who has passed through the heav[Eb]ens
Let us [Gm]hold fast to [Eb]our confession
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]The word of God is liv[F]ing and active
[Gm]Sharper than any two-[Eb]edged sword
